tadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The public HealthCheck result type exposes ok:boolean on every checks[] row while preserving status:ok|warn|fail; ok has one documented derivation from status and aggregate advisory/blocking policy remains unchanged; SDK, CLI JSON, MCP, compact/full projections, contracts, fixtures, and docs agree; compatibility tests prove existing status consumers are unchanged and naive row.ok predicates identify failures correctly; packaged npm/npx/bun/bunx acceptance, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, docstrings, and static gates pass"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make the public SDK health result self-consistent and safe for naive automation at every nesting level"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Agents can inspect failing health checks without silently inverting or disabling their gate predicate"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"SDK, CLI JSON, MCP, and extension consumers share one backward-compatible truth signal per check"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"The mismatch reproduces in current published packages and lies on the failure-investigation path used by release automation"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-usfg"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"GitHub #980"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"@unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.7, 2026.8.10, and 2026.8.11; Node 22; Linux"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Run pm health --json and compare top-level .ok with .checks[0].ok and .checks[0].status; .checks[0].ok is absent while status is ok"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Each checks[] entry carries a boolean ok compatible with the envelope spelling, alongside its existing tri-state status"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The e